<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iv" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-10">10 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Leo IV becomes pope after the death of Sergius II</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Leo IV succeeded Sergius II, whose pontificate had seen the Arab raid against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Leo repaired the churches damaged in the raid, built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonine-wall">Leonine Wall</a> around Vatican Hill and organised a league of Italian cities that won the sea <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ostia">Battle of Ostia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iv">Leo IV</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonine-wall">Leonine Wall</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ostia">Battle of Ostia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/damascus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damascus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-24">24 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake strikes Damascus, Antioch and Mosul</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A powerful earthquake, perhaps part of a multiple event stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>, struck <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. There were an estimated 20,000 casualties in Antioch, according to the historian al-Dhahabi, and 50,000 in Mosul.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch-on-the-orontes">Antioch-on-the-Orontes</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
